# Phase D.4 — GPU present for the DE compositor. When a virtio-gpu device is
# present the OVMF GOP is no longer the scanned-out surface (the driver did
# SET_SCANOUT to its own resource), so the SW GOP flush (fb_present_flush)
# reaches nothing; the device present is the ONLY live scanout path. This
# seam routes each finished damage rect through the device (BGRA backing +
# TRANSFER_TO_HOST + FLUSH) when active, else the SW GOP path is unchanged.
# devwsys -> vk_gpu -> virtio_gpu; no cycle (vk_gpu never imports devwsys).
# Phase D.5 — the shadow is composited BGRA-native when a device owns the
# scanout, so the flush is vk_de_present_shadow_rect_bgra: a pure 1:1 word-copy
# deposit + DMA (no per-pixel RGBA->BGRA convert). vk_gpu_backend_available()
# reports raw device presence (the gate for BGRA shadow, since under a device
# the SW GOP is already dead scanout).
